From a0a346e1a1453b5e7027bea14d18941967cf2c72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Ruhier <aruhier@mailbox.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:52:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hamoa: fix the aggre NoC clocks of
 usb_1_ss0

All the USB controllers DMA through the USB aggregate NoC, and all of
them but usb_1_ss0 hold GCC_AGGRE_NOC_USB_NORTH_AXI_CLK and
GCC_AGGRE_NOC_USB_SOUTH_AXI_CLK as "noc_aggr_north"/"noc_aggr_south".
usb_1_ss0 lists GCC_CFG_NOC_USB_ANOC_NORTH_AHB_CLK and
GCC_CFG_NOC_USB_ANOC_SOUTH_AHB_CLK under those names instead.

As long as another USB controller is active, the AXI clocks are on and
nothing shows. Once the others are runtime suspended, they are gated
while usb_1_ss0 is running: its registers are still reachable, but its
DMA stalls. On a Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x, plugging a keyboard into the
usb_1_ss0 port with the other controllers suspended left the xHC unable
to post the port change event or complete Enable Slot:

  xhci-hcd xhci-hcd.1.auto: Abort failed to stop command ring: -110
  xhci-hcd xhci-hcd.1.auto: xHCI host controller not responding, assume dead

Resuming another controller turned the clocks back on, and the stalled
write from usb_1_ss0 (SID 0x1420) completed at that moment.

Use the same NoC clocks as the other controllers.

Fixes: 4af46b7bd66f ("arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100: Add USB nodes")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
index 416a4badad0b1..577463350beb8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
@@ -5500,8 +5500,8 @@
 				 <&gcc GCC_USB30_PRIM_SLEEP_CLK>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_USB30_PRIM_MOCK_UTMI_CLK>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_AGGRE_USB_NOC_AXI_CLK>,
-				 <&gcc GCC_CFG_NOC_USB_ANOC_NORTH_AHB_CLK>,
-				 <&gcc GCC_CFG_NOC_USB_ANOC_SOUTH_AHB_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_AGGRE_NOC_USB_NORTH_AXI_CLK>,
+				 <&gcc GCC_AGGRE_NOC_USB_SOUTH_AXI_CLK>,
 				 <&gcc GCC_SYS_NOC_USB_AXI_CLK>;
 			clock-names = "cfg_noc",
 				      "core",
